{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And behold, a great dark terror was falling</b> — They derived from it a hint to the subjugation of the four exiles, for the prophet experienced in himself terror, and afterward darkness came, and afterward the darkness grew great, and afterward he felt as though it were falling upon him like a heavy burden weighing down upon him. They said (Genesis Rabbah 44:17): \"אֵימָה\" — this is Babylon; \"חֲשֵׁכָה\" — this is Media, for it darkened the eyes of Israel through fasting and affliction; \"גְדֹלָה\" — this is the kingdom of Antiochus; \"נֹפֶלֶת עָלָיו\" — this is Edom. And this matter was made known to Abraham because when the Holy One, blessed be He, established a covenant with him to give the land to his seed as an everlasting inheritance, He told him, as it were, in the very giving of His gift, that four exiles would enslave his sons and rule over their land — and this was on the condition that they would sin before Him. And afterward He made known to him another exile that would come first, namely the Egyptian exile, through which he had already been punished, as I have explained (Ramban on Genesis 12:10)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:45.142095196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}